# Fresh witnesses in generated rules
#
# Koko is an animal, and a rule turns that into two new rules. Each new rule
# says that some individual exists, a cat or a British shorthair, with a
# blank node. Eyeron introduces two distinct individuals, and a last rule
# confirms that they differ. It shows rules that conclude rules.

@prefix : <https://eyereasoner.github.io/ns#> .
@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#> .

:Koko a :Animal .

# A rule whose conclusion is two more rules. Each says: if Koko is an animal,
# some individual (_:x) is a cat, or a British shorthair. The two _:x are in
# different formulas, so they are different blank nodes.
{
    :Koko a :Animal
} => {
    {
        :Koko a :Animal
    } => {
        _:x a :Cat
    } .
    {
        :Koko a :Animal
    } => {
        _:x a :BritishShortHair
    } .
} .

# Succeeds when the cat and the shorthair are different individuals.
{
    ?X a :Cat .
    ?Y a :BritishShortHair .
    ?X log:notEqualTo ?Y .
} => {
    :test :is true .
} .
